### **Step-by-Step Solution:**

#### **1. Modify `appleSignInRequest` to Return Full Response:**

Instead of only returning the `identityToken`, modify the function to return the entire response so you can access the user's name and email.

```javascript
async function appleSignInRequest(): Promise<any> {
  try {
    const response = await appleAuth.performRequest({
      requestedOperation: appleAuth.Operation.LOGIN,
      requestedScopes: [appleAuth.Scope.FULL_NAME, appleAuth.Scope.EMAIL],
    });

    const credentialState = await appleAuth.getCredentialStateForUser(response.user);

    if (credentialState === appleAuth.State.AUTHORIZED) {
      return response; // Return the full response
    }

    console.log("[Apple Sign In] Authentication failed. Original response: ", {
      response,
    });
  } catch (error) {
    console.log("[Apple Sign In] Request failed:", error);
  }
}
```

